{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_rate_limit_middleware", "label": "Rate limit middleware (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "label": "rateLimit handler wrapper", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-key fixed-window limiter answering excess with 429 plus Retry-After; layered limits are composed by wrapping each handler with its own limiter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitoptions", "label": "RateLimitOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitcontext", "label": "RateLimitContext", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_key_function", "label": "key(request) derivation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Key on a value the client cannot forge \u2014 socket peer, user id, API key \u2014 never a raw x-forwarded-for, or an attacker rotates it per request to bypass the limit."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_fixed_window_counting", "label": "Fixed-window counting via cache incr with TTL", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The TTL on the counter is what makes fresh windows start cleanly; incr is atomic across pods when backed by Redis."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_fixed_window_edge_effects", "label": "Fixed-window edge effects", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A burst crossing a window boundary yields double the limit in seconds; no sliding-window or token-bucket variant ships, so implement one manually if strict burst protection matters."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_cluster_aware_rate_limiting", "label": "Cluster-aware rate limiting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Redis-backed cache shares one counter across pods; InMemoryCache gives each pod its own, so a client spread over 4 pods gets 4x the limit."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_dedicated_cache_instance", "label": "Do not share the limiter cache", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A flood travelling through the limiter can never evict its own counter, because incr runs before the max comparison and marks it most-recently-used. A key-minting route on the same Cache that the limiter does not wrap gives no such bump \u2014 measured on one shared maxEntries:4 instance, a client answered 429 was answered 200 again after twenty off-limiter Idempotency-Key requests."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_xforwardedfor_spoofing", "label": "Trusting X-Forwarded-For", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every common proxy appends, so whatever the client typed stays at the left of the header and keying on it is spoofable."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_rate_limit_middleware", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitoptions", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimitcontext", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_ratelimit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit_key_function", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/http/middleware/rate-limit.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_http_middleware_rate_limit